# AI-Fit Evaluator

Node 20+, ES modules. No frameworks, no database, no TypeScript, no agent libraries. Dependencies are only `@anthropic-ai/sdk`, `@tavily/core`, and `dotenv`.

Each module does one job and knows nothing about the others. Only `pipeline.js` wires them together.

- `src/llm.js`: `askJson({ system, user })` calls the model, requires JSON, parses it, retries once on invalid JSON. No knowledge of tools, search, or prompts.
- `src/prompts/*.js`: one file per step that builds prompt text. No API calls.
- `src/sheet.js`: `loadTools()` reads the internal tools Google Sheet and returns the array. No relevance logic. A different sheet source replaces only this file's internals.
- `src/search.js`: `search(query)` returns `{ title, url, snippet }[]`. No summarizing or judging.
- `src/steps/*.js`: one pipeline step each. Plain input in, plain object out. Do not print or read user input.
- `src/pipeline.js`: runs steps in order and holds state. Takes an `ask(question)` callback. No prompt text.
- `src/index.js`: CLI only. Reads and writes the terminal and supplies `ask`. No business logic.

Every LLM step returns JSON with a defined shape. The model must never invent tools: external options need a URL from actual search results, and internal matches must exist in the tools list.

Config comes from `.env` (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `TAVILY_API_KEY`). Fail with a clear message if either is missing.
